<!-- SECTION 3: WHAT IS GSTAT APPEAL FILING -->
<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What is a Turnover Certificate for Tender?</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>A turnover certificate for tender is a formal declaration issued by a practising Chartered Accountant on firm letterhead, certifying a business entity's gross annual turnover for one or more FYs based on examination of GST returns, Income Tax Returns, and audited financial statements, authenticated with an 18-digit UDIN from the ICAI portal to prevent forgery and enable online verification.</p><p>It serves as independent third-party validation of a bidder's financial capacity, enabling tendering authorities to filter non-serious or financially weak participants before technical evaluation. The CA examines books, reconciles turnover across GST (GSTR-3B/GSTR-9), ITR (Form ITR-3/5/6), and audited financials, and issues the certificate only after ensuring consistency. Any mismatch is reconciled through a clarification note.</p><p>For Gurugram businesses, this is a recurring compliance requirement - IT firms in Cyber City bidding on GeM, construction companies in Manesar competing for HSVP tenders, manpower agencies in Udyog Vihar responding to PSU tenders. Often bundled with <a href="/statutory-audit">Statutory Audit</a>, <a href="/gst-returns">GST Returns</a>, and <a href="/income-tax-return">Income Tax Return</a>.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for Turnover Certificate for Tender in Gurugram:</strong></p>
                    <ul><li><strong>UDIN:</strong> 18-digit ICAI number mandatory on all CA certificates since April 2019. First 6 = CA membership, next 6 = issue date, last 3 = serial</li><li><strong>GeM Portal (gem.gov.in):</strong> National public procurement portal. Turnover certificate with UDIN standard for seller onboarding and bid submission</li><li><strong>Haryana e-Procurement (etenders.hry.nic.in):</strong> State portal for HSVP, PWD, HUDA, HSIIDC, municipal tenders. Gurugram/Faridabad/Panipat</li><li><strong>Bid Capacity Certificate:</strong> CA certificate calculating max work value - required by PWD and CPWD construction tenders</li><li><strong>MAAT:</strong> Minimum Average Annual Turnover tender threshold - typically 30-100% of estimated contract value</li><li><strong>Section 2(91) IT Act:</strong> Turnover definition - aggregate realisation from sale, supply, distribution</li></ul>

                </div>
            </div>
