<!-- SECTION 15A: LEGAL FRAMEWORK -->
<section class="content-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">Turnover Certificate - Legal Framework</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                
                <p><strong>ICAI UDIN Requirement:</strong> UDIN mandatory for all CA certificates since April 2019. ICAI Council decision per Q28 of UDIN FAQ. 18-digit number from <a href="https://udin.icai.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">udin.icai.org</a>. Verifiable by any authority.</p><p><strong>Chartered Accountants Act, 1949:</strong> Only CA with valid Certificate of Practice (COP) from ICAI can issue turnover certificates. CS, CMA, other professionals cannot issue.</p><p><strong>Section 2(91) Income Tax Act:</strong> Turnover = aggregate realisation from sale/supply/distribution of goods/services. Basis for ITR turnover.</p><p><strong>Section 2(112) CGST Act 2017:</strong> Turnover = aggregate value of all taxable and non-taxable supplies (excluding reverse charge inward). Basis for GST turnover.</p><p><strong>GeM GTC:</strong> <a href="https://gem.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gem.gov.in</a> requires turnover certificate with UDIN for seller onboarding and bid submission.</p><p><strong>Haryana e-Procurement Policy:</strong> <a href="https://etenders.hry.nic.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">etenders.hry.nic.in</a> requires CA certificates with UDIN for tenders above threshold.</p><p><strong>Consequences:</strong> Fake UDIN or forged certificates - immediate bid rejection, 3-5 year blacklisting, Section 420 IPC (cheating). CA faces ICAI disciplinary action including membership removal.</p>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

